1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,280
If you walk away, don’t ever come back again, you brat!

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:06,320
You stop seeing that boy right now!

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:10,400
(Seeing their family fight because Bay and I
are together,)

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
I can’t help but feel guilty, Pa.

5
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:16,000
Just staying by my side

6
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:18,320
(and being cute like this is enough.)

7
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:22,040
I already know the truth about our family stealing Chun’s dim sum recipe.

8
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:23,720
(None of us did anything wrong.)

9
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,360
(I didn’t take Chun’s recipe)

10
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:28,120
(and you don’t have to feel guilty.)

11
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:29,000
Bee!

12
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:34,840
INCOMING CALL

13
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,160
Hello, mom.

14
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:46,400
(Bay, are you with your dad?
I don’t know where he went.)

15
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:49,360
Mom.

16
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:50,920
Did you find Dad?

17
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:51,640
I couldn’t find him.

18
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,360
-Urg, where is he?
-You couldn’t find him, either?

19
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:55,280
Obviously. And he’s not picking up his phone.

20
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
SUPPORTED BY THE DEPARTMENT OF CULTURAL PROMOTION,
MINISTRY OF CULTURE

21
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:31,400
I can’t eat anymore.

22
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,640
Woman Let’s pack it home then.

23
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:41,280
Italy, yay!

24
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:53,720
Let’s go.

25
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,040
Food waste.

26
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:07,840
What are you looking at, uncle?!

27
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,760
What’s up, son?!

28
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:14,960
I didn’t know I was your dad’s brother.

29
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,200
Watch your mouth, old man.

30
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:19,640
Scumbag! I’m not all talk.

31
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:21,520
You don’t wanna mess with me…

32
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,960
Son of a b*tch!

33
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:26,200
Sh*t! Why did you punch me?!

34
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:27,160
How about that, uncle?

35
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:28,720
How about this?!

36
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:32,760
Easy!

37
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,360
Hey!

38
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:47,360
Hey! Bay!

39
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,000
No!

40
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:54,120
Now hold on! Are you trying to murder him?!

41
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:54,920
Easy!

42
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:59,320
-Officer! Officer! Officer!
-Officer! Officer!

43
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:00,760
-Let’s go!
-There’s a fight over here!

44
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:01,480
Get lost!

45
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:04,120
-Bay!
-Bay!

46
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:06,280
Are you alright?

47
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,760
Why did you pick a fight with those guys?

48
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,920
You’re lucky we got there in time!

49
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:23,440
Bay.

50
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,520
I think we all should get some rest, son.

51
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,200
We can’t solve anything until everyone’s calmed down.

52
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:37,080
You’re his Pa now?

53
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:40,440
His damn Pa?

54
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:44,360
Great. Take everything from me.

55
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:46,760
Can you stop being a jerk?

56
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,320
No one has the energy to fight with you anymore.

57
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:53,800
Why don’t you stop babbling and get out of my face?

58
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,480
You need to stop.

59
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:59,960
Everyone risked their lives to save you today.

60
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Don’t you have any gratitude?

61
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:05,200
You’re acting crazy and trying to control everyone

62
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:08,520
because you want to justify yourself, right?

63
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:14,240
That you weren’t wrong when you chose to betray Chun back then.

64
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,480
Am I right?

65
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:28,640
I’m sorry, Chun.

66
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:33,400
I’m sorry, kids.

67
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:35,800
I knew everything.

68
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:40,000
But I never tried to make it right.

69
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:50,680
If you want any compensation,

70
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:53,080
we’ll take responsibility for it.

71
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,680
If you call it quits, I’ll do the same.

72
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:15,720
I don’t want to take anything from you.

73
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:20,880
I only want you to leave me and my son alone. That’s all.

74
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:34,200
Tell Chun you’re sorry.

75
00:06:34,840 --> 00:06:38,000
And just let Bay and Boat be.

76
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:42,840
Or else…

77
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:47,320
our marriage is over.

78
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:51,640
Honey…

79
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:55,480
Do you have to go that far?

80
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:57,600
Damn it.

81
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,360
I’ll go live with Mom.

82
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:11,280
Me, too.

83
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:16,920
What are you guys talking about?

84
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:21,800
Do you hate your dad that much? Huh?

85
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:23,600
Boat.

86
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:28,360
Honey.

87
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:37,080
You’re luckier than me
that you still have a chance.

88
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:07,360
I’m sorry, Chun

89
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:11,800
I’m sorry.

90
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:25,560
Bay,

91
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:29,880
I’m sorry, son.

92
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:32,920
I’m sorry, Boat

93
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:37,840
I’m sorry, honey.

94
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:39,560
I’m sorry.

95
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:41,800
I’m sorry.

96
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:49,040
I’m sorry.

97
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:57,840
I’m sorry.

98
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,360
I really am.

99
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:07,240
This looks worse than I thought.

100
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:13,040
Are you sure you’re okay?

101
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:18,840
I’m okay.

102
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,040
Don’t worry about me.

103
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,960
You should go to sleep.

104
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:28,320
I don’t think I can.

105
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:31,960
Fortunately,

106
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:35,080
the tryout is in the evening.

107
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:42,960
Come get some sleep.

108
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:15,200
I can’t wait to fall asleep and wake up tomorrow.

109
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:17,160
Why?

110
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,200
Tomorrow, you’ll get to be in the national team.

111
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:25,280
And you and I will finally get to be together.

112
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:29,600
I’ve been waiting for this for so long, Son.

113
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:32,960
You…

114
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,840
don’t think there’s a chance I won’t make it?

115
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:37,640
No.

116
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:41,240
I always know you can do it.

117
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,440
I knew since we were eight.

118
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:51,280
Good night.

119
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:52,880
Good night

120
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:34,960
-Can I sleep on your pillow?
-Come on.

121
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:59,400
CLOSED FOR ONE DAY.
GONE TO SUPPORT MY SON

122
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:01,760
BUSINESS CLOSED

123
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:04,440
What are you smiling about, Chun?

124
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,520
I’m just closing for renovations.

125
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:08,680
I’ll reopen with an even better shop.

126
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:13,520
Now that you’re fixing your shop,
why don’t you fix your attitude as well?

127
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:14,520
Fine.

128
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:17,160
I’ll be back with a brand-new attitude.

129
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:19,920
I’ll come up with an idea for my new shop.

130
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
I guarantee my business will kick your business’s ass.

131
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:24,120
It’ll be so good you’ll have to close your place down.

132
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:26,600
Why don’t you change the recipe for your dim sum, too?

133
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:29,520
You’ve been selling the same damn thing for a century.

134
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:30,600
Ptui!

135
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:36,560
TENNIS NATIONAL TEAM TRYOUT COMPETITION

136
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:50,240
You’ll start playing after the first match is over.

137
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:53,200
It should be around 7 PM. Please warm up beforehand.

138
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:54,840
-Okay.
-Yes.

139
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:18,600
Bay!

140
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,240
Bay!

141
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:23,600
Bay!

142
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,160
Bay!

143
00:13:26,520 --> 00:13:26,960
Bay!

144
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:28,560
Bay!

145
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:40,200
(Based on what you’ve told me and the ECG results,)

146
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:43,800
it may have been caused by a severe blow to the chest from a hard object,

147
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:46,960
which caused his heart rhythm to become irregular.

148
00:13:47,440 --> 00:13:49,680
For now, I’ve given him medication intravenously.

149
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:51,040
If you’ll excuse me.

150
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:52,240
Thank you.

151
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:05,680
I don’t think I can do this, Coach.

152
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:08,680
Sun, take a deep breath.

153
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:11,400
How can I focus while playing?

154
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:14,680
The match is about to start.

155
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:16,720
You have to believe you can do it.

156
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:19,480
Sun.

157
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:28,560
If Bay found out he was the reason you missed your chance, it would destroy him.

158
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:33,560
Sun, can you keep fighting?

159
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:37,600
Can you please do this for Bay?

160
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:06,520
Come on, Sun.

161
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:07,920
Sun, let’s go.

162
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:08,960
You’ve got this, Sun.

163
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:17,480
Damn, why does it have to be today?

164
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:21,200
Sun needs to win 2 more sets to get into the national team.

165
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:23,600
The opponent has scored really well.

166
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:25,880
Will Sun be able to do this?

167
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:28,640
If he wants to play professionally,

168
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:32,360
he has to do it, even if he has to play through his tears.

169
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:34,120
Ready?

170
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:37,280
Are you okay?

171
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:41,320
I’m ready.

172
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:43,000
Let’s begin then.

173
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:02,400
Hey.

174
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,640
It’s okay, son.

175
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,000
Come back. Come back.

176
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:12,760
It’s alright. You’re still good.

177
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:35,000
It’s okay, son. It’s okay.

178
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:39,920
Sun, Bay is in good hands.

179
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:40,960
Don’t worry.

180
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:45,440
I want you to focus only on this match, okay?

181
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:48,000
I know it’s hard

182
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:52,160
but I believe you can do this.

183
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:55,280
Go, Sun.

184
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:58,880
Sun, you’ve got this. Come on.

185
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:23,880
(Sun.)

186
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:28,320
If our dads still try to keep us apart like this,

187
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,800
when you’re competing in the national tryout,

188
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:33,080
I won’t be able to be there for you.

189
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:35,200
It’s okay.

190
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,240
Really?

191
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:40,160
Really.

192
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:42,520
Damn.

193
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:45,440
It’s not important if I’m there or not?

194
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,480
Of course, it is.

195
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:51,360
But there will be times when you can’t be there to cheer me on, right?

196
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:54,720
Like when you’re studying abroad.

197
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:02,280
If I held this against you,

198
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:04,520
how could we go on as a couple?

199
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:13,120
But I want you to know I’ll be cheering for you,

200
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:18,360
thinking about how well you’re playing,

201
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:22,480
concerning if you’re ahead or behind.

202
00:18:23,280 --> 00:18:24,920
Just like when we played together.

203
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:27,960
I know.

204
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:33,840
Ugh, I still want to be there to cheer for you.

205
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:39,560
How about this?

206
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:43,960
I’ll keep playing tennis for a long time.

207
00:18:44,440 --> 00:18:46,960
Until the day you come back to cheer me on in person.

208
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:49,120
Okay?

209
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:54,320
Okay, I’ll hurry back so I can cheer you on.

210
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:01,520
While I’m not there, just know I’m trying my best
to come back for you.

211
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:07,240
♪ It’s time that we fall in love ♪

212
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:12,760
♪ It’s finally time for you and me to be in love ♪

213
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:15,920
♪ This very second belongs to you alone ♪

214
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:18,920
♪ My heartbeat says it's yours to own ♪

215
00:19:23,800 --> 00:19:24,560
Let’s go, Sun.

216
00:19:42,840 --> 00:19:44,360
-Yay!
-That’s it!

217
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:56,040
-Yes!
-Woo!

218
00:19:56,080 --> 00:19:58,000
Sun is back.

219
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:00,360
Good job, son. Let’s go.

220
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:10,680
-Yeah!
-Yes!

221
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:13,040
-Nice job
-Nice job

222
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:13,760
Nice job, Sun.

223
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:15,320
Good job.

224
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:39,920
-Go.
-Let’s go.

225
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:40,760
Almost there, Sun.

226
00:20:41,120 --> 00:20:41,920
Give it your best shot.

227
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:43,440
Focus, Sun, focus.

228
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:58,040
(While I’m not there, just know I’m trying my best
to come back for you.)

229
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:21,160
Yay!

230
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:21,680
Yes!

231
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:29,320
Yay!

232
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:30,400
Fantastic!

233
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:33,000
It’s Match point, son. Hang in there.

234
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:34,720
Just one more, Sun. One more.

235
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:36,360
Almost there.

236
00:21:36,360 --> 00:21:37,280
Come on, Sun.

237
00:21:58,520 --> 00:21:59,880
Yay!!

238
00:21:59,880 --> 00:22:02,280
Yay!

239
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:03,680
Yay!

240
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:11,320
Amazing!

241
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:12,120
Great job!

242
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:15,040
-Well done!
-Amazing!

243
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:15,560
Sun!

244
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:17,440
Bay’s awake.

245
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:20,080
-What? Really?
-Bay’s awake.

246
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:27,080
-(Yay!)
-(Woo!)

247
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:30,280
Bay!

248
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:40,760
You really did it. Nice job.

249
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:51,640
You’re not hurt anymore?

250
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:53,960
Mmm, I’m okay now.

251
00:22:58,320 --> 00:22:59,360
You sure?

252
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,760
Don’t do this to me again.

253
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:11,880
I don’t want to, either.

254
00:23:12,920 --> 00:23:14,680
I feel so bad.

255
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:16,680
I didn’t get to watch you play.

256
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:18,760
Don’t worry about it.

257
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:21,920
You had to recover.

258
00:23:23,040 --> 00:23:24,360
But I’ve seen you on the phone.

259
00:23:24,560 --> 00:23:25,680
You did great.

260
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:30,200
-Promise?
-I promise. I promise.

261
00:23:39,080 --> 00:23:42,400
Congratulations to all students graduating today.

262
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:45,720
From now on, you get to follow the path
you chose for yourselves.

263
00:23:46,120 --> 00:23:47,760
But l’d like you to know

264
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:48,960
CALCULUS, MY TOFU
I’m always here to support you.

265
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:50,640
I’m always here to support you.

266
00:23:51,560 --> 00:23:53,240
I wish you all good luck.

267
00:23:56,920 --> 00:23:59,400
Hey, I got into the Faculty of Fine Arts.

268
00:23:59,520 --> 00:24:02,120
-Wait. Are you serious?
-Yeah.

269
00:24:02,120 --> 00:24:04,040
-Damn. I’m happy for you.
-Thanks, buddy.

270
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:04,760
So cool.

271
00:24:05,760 --> 00:24:08,000
And what about you going to Italy?

272
00:24:19,880 --> 00:24:21,280
Why did you take me here?

273
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:26,720
Since we’ve gone public, we barely came here anymore.

274
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:33,560
I have something to tell you.

275
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,360
I got accepted by a school in Italy.

276
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:01,440
And what did your parents say?

277
00:25:04,600 --> 00:25:05,560
I’ve talked to them

278
00:25:11,520 --> 00:25:12,320
and they said yes.

279
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:15,720
They did?!

280
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:17,920
You’ll really get to study abroad?

281
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:23,280
And you’re really okay with that?

282
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:30,240
-If you’re not, I can go to a university here…
-You have to go.

283
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,400
You have to.

284
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:38,280
You’re not sad at all?

285
00:25:42,800 --> 00:25:44,440
You seem more excited than I am.

286
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:50,680
What’s there to be sad about?

287
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:54,920
You go do what you love over there.

288
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:58,800
And I’ll do what I love over here.

289
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:03,320
When the time comes, we’ll get to be together again.

290
00:26:03,880 --> 00:26:04,640
That’s all.

291
00:26:06,440 --> 00:26:08,040
And you’re not afraid we’re gonna break up?

292
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:12,960
We don’t have to.

293
00:26:14,560 --> 00:26:18,400
Didn’t you say it yourself
that even though we weren’t together,

294
00:26:19,640 --> 00:26:21,560
you’d still be cheering me on from there.

295
00:26:23,800 --> 00:26:25,240
A good love

296
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:28,440
should be pushing you forward

297
00:26:29,480 --> 00:26:30,840
not holding you back.

298
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:38,440
And…I’ll be supporting you from here, too.

299
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:43,200
You are so adorable.

300
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:45,360
You should adore me then.

301
00:26:46,160 --> 00:26:47,840
I adore you.

302
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:50,720
Who wouldn’t love you, my little tofu?

303
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:55,360
We should’ve started dating when we were eight

304
00:26:55,640 --> 00:26:57,840
so we had more time together before I leave.

305
00:26:58,560 --> 00:26:59,680
Are you crazy?

306
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:02,440
You’re so silly.

307
00:27:04,520 --> 00:27:05,200
Woo!

308
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:18,040
-Let’s share.
-What’d you wanna eat?

309
00:27:18,080 --> 00:27:18,800
Want some?

310
00:27:18,800 --> 00:27:20,040
-You want it?
-Want some?

311
00:27:20,040 --> 00:27:21,920
-Here comes the pizza.
-No, I’m good.

312
00:27:22,200 --> 00:27:25,000
-Here’s the pizza.
-Thank you.

313
00:27:25,160 --> 00:27:26,960
-Come on.
-Here we go.

314
00:27:27,040 --> 00:27:28,360
-Share it.
-I’ll go first.

315
00:27:28,360 --> 00:27:30,280
That table, take this.

316
00:27:31,960 --> 00:27:34,120
Hey, Bay, can you speak Italian?

317
00:27:34,760 --> 00:27:37,400
-Of course, bonjour.
-Bonjour my ass.

318
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:41,800
You jerk. I’ll poke you with a fork.
Watch it.

319
00:27:41,800 --> 00:27:43,040
There’s only one slide left?

320
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:44,120
Yeah.

321
00:27:44,600 --> 00:27:48,520
-Where’s mine?
-You’ll be in Italy. You can eat pizza every day.

322
00:27:48,520 --> 00:27:51,840
-What the hell? I wanna eat it.
-Do you want mine?

323
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:52,480
Hey.

324
00:27:53,520 --> 00:27:55,480
I’m okay. You eat it, babe.

325
00:27:55,480 --> 00:27:58,480
What’s with the baby voice?

326
00:27:58,480 --> 00:28:01,040
-“You eat it, babe”, he said.
-What are you talking about?

327
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:05,080
-You’ve never sweet talked to me like that.
-Why? You’re not my boyfriend.

328
00:28:05,120 --> 00:28:06,000
Or do you want to be?

329
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:09,840
I’m just kidding.

330
00:28:10,360 --> 00:28:12,440
I’ll take the left-over home.

331
00:28:12,560 --> 00:28:14,200
What are you whispering about?

332
00:28:14,840 --> 00:28:15,920
I brought you pizza.

333
00:28:16,120 --> 00:28:20,200
I didn’t have to, Boat. We got plenty of food here.

334
00:28:20,640 --> 00:28:21,880
Boat loves his pizza.

335
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:25,720
He has tried all the pizza around the country.

336
00:28:25,960 --> 00:28:28,560
He wanted to eat some today so he ordered it. Right?

337
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:30,880
-You know me, Dad.
-I sure do.

338
00:28:31,360 --> 00:28:33,000
If your son loves pizza that much,

339
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:34,840
why don’t you open a pizza shop?

340
00:28:40,480 --> 00:28:42,680
-You two, enjoy. I’ll be outside
-Okay

341
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:48,160
Is this edible?

342
00:28:53,240 --> 00:28:54,400
Wanna try some?

343
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:58,000
If it’s not good, I’ll let you kick me in the face.

344
00:28:58,080 --> 00:29:01,680
Can I kick you first and then I’ll try it?

345
00:29:01,880 --> 00:29:02,880
Look at you.

346
00:29:05,040 --> 00:29:06,360
This is life changing.

347
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:08,560
You go girl.

348
00:29:09,600 --> 00:29:11,120
Go, go, go.

349
00:29:13,720 --> 00:29:14,400
Yay!

350
00:29:16,480 --> 00:29:18,440
You’re making me blush.

351
00:29:31,640 --> 00:29:33,360
Have the kids been drinking?

352
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:35,280
It’s just their personality.

353
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:38,440
They’ve had a whole box of soda.

354
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:40,040
I think they’re drunk on sugar.

355
00:29:41,320 --> 00:29:42,880
Will I ever get to see you two again?

356
00:29:43,360 --> 00:29:45,200
You’ll be studying abroad.

357
00:29:45,440 --> 00:29:47,000
And you’ll be with the national team.

358
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:48,440
You’ll forget about me.

359
00:29:49,040 --> 00:29:51,440
No way. How can I forget you?

360
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:53,120
-Really.
-Really.

361
00:29:53,280 --> 00:29:57,960
You’ll see. I’ll be the best club leader.

362
00:29:58,120 --> 00:30:00,000
And I will be the next PREM’S GAME champion.

363
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:03,560
Because I was there during your era and I got to play with you.

364
00:30:03,600 --> 00:30:05,600
Bro, that’s fierce.

365
00:30:05,800 --> 00:30:08,200
Hey, I won’t allow that.

366
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:09,560
What the hell?

367
00:30:09,560 --> 00:30:12,960
-If you want to hug someone, go hug Petong.
-What?

368
00:30:13,040 --> 00:30:15,240
Go hug Petong. Stop it.

369
00:30:15,280 --> 00:30:20,920
What? No, stop it.

370
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:22,040
No.

371
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:26,600
I’ve always considered you a friend.

372
00:30:26,760 --> 00:30:30,040
I know. My friend, Chun.

373
00:30:30,040 --> 00:30:33,800
My bestie. My ride or die.

374
00:30:34,080 --> 00:30:37,680
Wow. “My ride or die”, he said?

375
00:30:40,720 --> 00:30:42,040
They’re in love.

376
00:30:46,080 --> 00:30:50,800
Are you still sad seeing these kids graduate?

377
00:30:54,040 --> 00:30:57,080
Well…I am a little.

378
00:30:58,040 --> 00:31:00,400
But this year, I feel a bit better.

379
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:01,840
How?

380
00:31:03,200 --> 00:31:06,240
It’s because…

381
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:09,920
you’re not leaving with them.

382
00:31:16,320 --> 00:31:17,280
I mean…

383
00:31:17,840 --> 00:31:21,520
You can keep me company so I won’t get lonely.

384
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:25,080
You’re all talk.

385
00:31:25,960 --> 00:31:28,240
You’d better not leave me and go date someone.

386
00:31:30,920 --> 00:31:31,520
Why?

387
00:31:32,360 --> 00:31:34,960
Why can’t I date someone?

388
00:31:38,320 --> 00:31:39,360
No reason.

389
00:31:41,480 --> 00:31:42,760
I just won’t allow it.

390
00:31:47,760 --> 00:31:48,560
Hey, wait.

391
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:51,680
You idiot.

392
00:31:53,560 --> 00:31:57,520
-That’s crazy.
-Oh, hell no. Hell no.

393
00:31:57,520 --> 00:31:59,040
Hey, girl.

394
00:32:03,720 --> 00:32:05,000
Wait, hold on.

395
00:32:08,200 --> 00:32:09,360
You should bring one more luggage.

396
00:32:09,800 --> 00:32:14,200
No, I won’t. I’ve got too much stuff already.

397
00:32:16,360 --> 00:32:17,840
But there’s still room for you to get in.

398
00:32:18,360 --> 00:32:19,840
Wanna come with me?

399
00:32:23,640 --> 00:32:24,680
Funny.

400
00:32:27,800 --> 00:32:30,480
Try sitting on it. That might work.

401
00:32:33,120 --> 00:32:33,960
Damn.

402
00:32:36,360 --> 00:32:38,800
-There. Close it.
-Yes.

403
00:32:40,080 --> 00:32:40,960
Finally.

404
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:46,480
Took you long enough. Shouldn’t have spent your time playing games.

405
00:32:47,160 --> 00:32:48,120
Before I leave,

406
00:32:48,880 --> 00:32:50,880
let’s review our deal one more time.

407
00:32:53,200 --> 00:32:56,800
-Well…we’ll text each other every day.
-Mmm.

408
00:32:57,160 --> 00:33:00,240
If there’s a problem or misunderstanding,

409
00:33:00,880 --> 00:33:02,080
we’ll talk it out right away.

410
00:33:02,840 --> 00:33:03,640
That’s right.

411
00:33:04,160 --> 00:33:04,880
What about Sundays?

412
00:33:05,080 --> 00:33:06,120
Video calls.

413
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:10,320
I’ve put you on my schedule for the next three years.

414
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:12,000
Good boy.

415
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:14,280
What if someone hits on you?

416
00:33:16,160 --> 00:33:18,240
If someone hits on me,

417
00:33:22,040 --> 00:33:26,600
-I’ll feed them to the crocodile.
-Good boy.

418
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:30,600
You should stop teaching me to be weird like you.

419
00:33:30,640 --> 00:33:31,440
I can’t.

420
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:34,000
I don’t want you to be cute with other people.

421
00:33:34,240 --> 00:33:36,480
I had to teach you to be a little weird, okay?

422
00:33:37,320 --> 00:33:39,680
My tofu.

423
00:33:39,800 --> 00:33:40,600
Oww.

424
00:33:43,520 --> 00:33:44,640
Let’s go now.

425
00:33:46,080 --> 00:33:48,880
Ready? One…two…three.

426
00:33:55,280 --> 00:33:57,080
I know I’ll miss you so much.

427
00:34:09,200 --> 00:34:11,200
I know I’ll miss you more.

428
00:34:43,200 --> 00:34:45,720
♪ Ever since that day ♪

429
00:34:46,640 --> 00:34:52,360
♪ When you and I happened to meet,
it’s like a dream ♪

430
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:53,880
♪ ’Cause you’re the one ♪

431
00:34:53,880 --> 00:34:57,480
♪ Who came along and made my heart skip a beat ♪

432
00:34:57,840 --> 00:35:04,680
♪ It feels like I’ve finally found love ♪

433
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:11,480
1 YEAR LATER

434
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:21,640
That’s all. Drive safely.

435
00:35:28,560 --> 00:35:31,960
-2 boxes of Hawaiian pizza. Thank you so much.
-Yes.

436
00:35:34,040 --> 00:35:35,600
Hey, Bee!

437
00:35:35,880 --> 00:35:37,600
Don’t you know how to manage your shop?

438
00:35:37,720 --> 00:35:38,480
SAMING PHON FAI
Look.

439
00:35:38,720 --> 00:35:41,240
Your customers are standing on the street.

440
00:35:41,360 --> 00:35:43,080
What, Chun?

441
00:35:43,200 --> 00:35:45,960
You’re jealous of me already?

442
00:35:45,960 --> 00:35:46,960
Why would I be?

443
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:48,040
I got lots of customers, too.

444
00:35:48,040 --> 00:35:48,800
Where?

445
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:50,600
I can only count like 10 people.

446
00:35:50,720 --> 00:35:52,120
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

447
00:35:52,160 --> 00:35:53,400
Are you freaking blind?

448
00:35:53,400 --> 00:35:56,120
See how long my line is?

449
00:35:56,160 --> 00:35:57,560
I got online orders, too.

450
00:35:57,560 --> 00:36:00,360
-What’s wrong? Why are you standing like that?
-Pa, enough.

451
00:36:01,160 --> 00:36:02,240
-Pa.
-What?

452
00:36:02,400 --> 00:36:04,280
Your customers are hangry.

453
00:36:04,280 --> 00:36:06,880
-Damn.
-For my customers’ sake.

454
00:36:06,880 --> 00:36:09,560
You’re gonna lose your customers because you’re so cocky.

455
00:36:09,560 --> 00:36:11,640
What? What does that even mean?

456
00:36:11,800 --> 00:36:15,480
-I have a business to run.
-Yeah, I have a business to run, too.

457
00:36:15,520 --> 00:36:17,200
Please, come in. This way.

458
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:32,840
Sun!

459
00:36:54,560 --> 00:36:55,160
Hey!

460
00:36:55,800 --> 00:36:56,560
Bay!

461
00:36:57,440 --> 00:36:58,400
Damn.

462
00:36:59,160 --> 00:37:00,120
You beat me again.

463
00:37:01,760 --> 00:37:02,920
What are you doing here?

464
00:37:03,720 --> 00:37:05,160
Why didn’t you tell me you were coming?

465
00:37:05,440 --> 00:37:07,000
I wanted to surprise you.

466
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:09,360
You’re going to give a speech.

467
00:37:09,520 --> 00:37:10,800
How could I miss it?

468
00:37:11,200 --> 00:37:12,960
-No way.
-Why?

469
00:37:13,200 --> 00:37:14,800
You came back just watch me give a speech?

470
00:37:15,480 --> 00:37:17,520
Fine, I’ll tell you the truth.

471
00:37:18,360 --> 00:37:19,280
My university is on break.

472
00:37:20,120 --> 00:37:21,480
So I’ll stay here for a month.

473
00:37:24,880 --> 00:37:25,680
Are you serious?

474
00:37:26,480 --> 00:37:27,160
Of course.

475
00:37:29,520 --> 00:37:31,000
Why didn’t you tell me first?

476
00:37:33,760 --> 00:37:34,960
Do you miss me that much?

477
00:37:35,680 --> 00:37:36,640
Of course I do.

478
00:37:37,680 --> 00:37:39,080
I haven’t seen you for so long.

479
00:37:39,560 --> 00:37:40,720
When we talked on the phone,

480
00:37:41,120 --> 00:37:42,560
you always acted tough.

481
00:37:43,240 --> 00:37:47,000
Seeing how much you miss me, I’m relieved.

482
00:37:47,560 --> 00:37:49,200
My tofu.

483
00:37:49,520 --> 00:37:52,440
Hey, Bay, you can’t pinch my cheek in public.

484
00:37:52,560 --> 00:37:55,480
I’m a national athlete now.

485
00:37:55,640 --> 00:37:56,720
What if someone sees me?

486
00:37:57,480 --> 00:37:59,320
-See?
-Mmm.

487
00:37:59,400 --> 00:38:00,640
See this flag?

488
00:38:00,640 --> 00:38:02,920
Fine. I’ll stop doing that.

489
00:38:04,120 --> 00:38:06,800
Pinching my cheek like that… I’m embarrassed.

490
00:38:08,560 --> 00:38:09,120
Hey!

491
00:38:12,440 --> 00:38:14,320
Did you just kiss my cheek?

492
00:38:14,680 --> 00:38:15,440
You’re shy?

493
00:38:20,560 --> 00:38:21,040
A little bit.

494
00:38:22,760 --> 00:38:23,640
And do you like it?

495
00:38:32,400 --> 00:38:32,880
Yes.

496
00:38:41,080 --> 00:38:41,960
Come on. Let’s go to school.

497
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:44,040
You’re shy, huh?

498
00:38:45,680 --> 00:38:46,240
What?

499
00:38:47,440 --> 00:38:51,000
Next, I’d like to invite one of our alumni to come up and give a speech.

500
00:38:57,960 --> 00:39:00,640
Good morning, everyone. My name’s Sun.

501
00:39:00,840 --> 00:39:02,000
I’m an alumnus of this school.

502
00:39:02,520 --> 00:39:05,840
How are you feeling on the last day of your high school life?

503
00:39:06,120 --> 00:39:06,920
Are you glad?

504
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:10,480
Or are you worried about something?

505
00:39:10,480 --> 00:39:11,560
I’m so glad.

506
00:39:11,560 --> 00:39:14,200
I’m excited.

507
00:39:18,480 --> 00:39:23,800
I used to be so afraid of change and saying goodbye.

508
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:32,240
Until I learned that every ending
is also a new beginning.

509
00:39:33,520 --> 00:39:38,520
I thought being an athlete made me understand that.

510
00:39:39,160 --> 00:39:43,760
Because finishing one game
means you’re starting another.

511
00:39:45,200 --> 00:39:46,280
But that wasn’t the reason.

512
00:39:51,440 --> 00:39:53,600
I realized those things weren’t scary

513
00:39:55,680 --> 00:39:57,560
when I received genuine love

514
00:39:59,920 --> 00:40:01,000
from the people in my life.

515
00:40:05,240 --> 00:40:07,480
(My son came up with the pizza dough recipe himself.)

516
00:40:07,560 --> 00:40:08,400
(It was love)

517
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:12,600
APPLICATION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM UNIVERSITY
(that made me realize I didn’t have to be someone else to be loved.)

518
00:40:13,640 --> 00:40:15,640
I’ve got a new pizza recipe for you to try.

519
00:40:28,920 --> 00:40:31,040
YOU ARE CORDIALLY INVITED TO CELEBRATE OUR WEDDING

520
00:40:31,280 --> 00:40:34,840
(Love that will never change even when we do.)

521
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:38,840
I like the tennis term ‘love-all’.

522
00:40:39,440 --> 00:40:43,640
‘Love’ sounds a bit like the French word for zero.

523
00:40:45,480 --> 00:40:47,400
It’s used when a new game begins.

524
00:40:49,160 --> 00:40:51,400
Our lives are not so different from a tennis match.

525
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:54,480
BUSINESS CLOSED

526
00:40:54,640 --> 00:40:56,240
(I’d like all of you to believe)

527
00:40:56,560 --> 00:40:59,480
(that every ending always has a new beginning waiting for you.)

528
00:41:00,600 --> 00:41:02,600
Hello, Sun. What are you doing?

529
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:03,760
Taking a break.

530
00:41:04,160 --> 00:41:06,000
-Is it raining there?
-(But genuine love)

531
00:41:06,520 --> 00:41:10,840
-Yeah, it’s just started to drizzle.
-(makes the journey to your new beginning less scary.)

532
00:41:11,920 --> 00:41:14,080
And when your new match begins,

533
00:41:15,360 --> 00:41:17,400
shout, “Love-all” and start to play.

534
00:41:29,280 --> 00:41:31,280
HE WAS RAISED WELL, HIS PASSION SHINES BRIGHT,
FACE CARD NEVER DECLINED, OMG, GREAT SPEECH!

535
00:41:38,600 --> 00:41:39,800
Sun’s speech was inspiring.

